<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A score input built from a row of stars - or any icon pair - with support for fractional values.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/rating)

<%= embed AppicaUI::RatingPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Rating(default_value: 3, aria_label: "Rate this product")
Rating(name: "score", clearable: true, aria_labelledby: "score-label")      # submits with a form
Rating(value: 4.3, step: 0.1, read_only: true, size: 14, class: "text-warning-emphasis")
```

A `radiogroup` of icon buttons that fills from the start of the row up to the value. Moving the pointer previews the
rating a click would set (snapped to `step`) and lifts the icon under it; a click commits it. The group is one tab
stop: ←/→/↑/↓ step by `step` (←/→ swap under RTL), Home/End jump to the ends, Space/Enter select the focused item.
The fill is rendered on the server (a `--rating-fill` per item), so read-only ratings need no JavaScript. The accent
is the text color (`text-primary` by default). Every animation honors `prefers-reduced-motion`.

