## API reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `value:` / `default_value:` | `Numeric` | - / `0` | The rating (0 = unrated). |
| `count:` | `Integer` | `5` | Number of items. |
| `step:` | `Numeric` | `1` | Smallest selectable fraction (`0.5` for halves). A finer value renders exactly. |
| `icon:` | `Symbol`, `{ empty:, filled: }` | `:star` | Icon pair. |
| `variant:` | `:filled`, `:outline` | `:filled` | Unrated items as muted solid icons, or line icons in the accent. |
| `orientation:` | `:horizontal`, `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | A vertical rating fills from the top down. |
| `size:` | `Integer` (px), `String` | `24` | Icon size; any CSS length (`"1em"` follows the text). Padding is a sixth of it. |
| `hoverable:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Preview the rating under the pointer. |
| `clearable:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Selecting the current rating again resets it to 0. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Blocks interaction and dims the control. |
| `read_only:` | `Boolean` | `false` | A non-interactive display, exposed as one labelled image. |
| `name:` | `String` | - | Hidden input submitted with a form. |

Attributes like `aria_label:` / `aria_labelledby:` go to the root; `class:` is merged (set the accent there).
Events: `appica-ui--rating:change` and `appica-ui--rating:hover-change`, both with `{ value }`.

## Accessibility

- Interactive: `role="radiogroup"` with a `role="radio"` button per item, named "3 of 5" (translated); name the
  group with `aria_label:` or `aria_labelledby:` (it's "Rating" otherwise).
- Fractional values are announced at item granularity; `read_only:` exposes the exact average as one image
  ("4.3 out of 5", in the current locale).
- The hover sweep, lift and press animations are skipped under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
